This means 81% of students like either blue, green, or both. To find the percentage of students who like neither, we subtract this from 100%:
\[ P(\text{neither}) = 100\% - P(B \cup G) = 100\% - 81\% = 19\% \]

So, the probability that a randomly picked student would like neither blue nor green is 19%.

