   - **Monetary Policy**: This involves the use of interest rates and the money supply by central banks to influence the economy. Monetary policy can be used to control inflation (e.g., by raising interest rates to reduce borrowing and spending) or to stimulate economic growth (e.g., by lowering interest rates to encourage borrowing and spending).

